implementationPlan.description:
Host side.

(a) scripts/local-runner/snapshot-transfer.mjs:
- MODES becomes ['materialize', 'export', 'verify'].
- Export verifyWorkspace({ name, provider = {}, timeoutMs } = {}), modeled on materializeSnapshot:
  - snapshotArgv(name, 'verify') refuses a non-owned name before any spawn;
  - assertNoMounts before and after;
  - runSupervisorStream with input [] and an onFrame that accepts exactly ONE frame with exact keys {changed, kind}, kind 'verified', and changed a non-negative safe integer. Anything else throws TRANSFER_FRAME_INVALID, as materializeSnapshot's onFrame does. No frame also throws TRANSFER_FRAME_INVALID.
  - Resolve 'intact' when changed is 0, else 'changed'.
- No snapshot argument: the guest compares against its own root-only manifest, written by this run's materialize, which the host already checked by digest.

(b) scripts/local-runner/check-lifecycle.mjs, created by CQ-R11 (task-07951125); edit its LANDED bytes:
- runCheckJob's dependency argument gains verify = verifyWorkspace;
- after the session and BEFORE remove, and only when session.outcome === 'passed', set workspace = await verify({ name, provider, timeoutMs });
- a rejection, or any value other than 'intact' or 'changed', leaves 'unverified';
- every other path keeps 'unverified';
- update its header comment, which said workspace is always 'unverified'.
The delete-before-settle and every other R11 rule are unchanged.

VERIFY ONCE, fresh.

1. Run the DoD command, `node --test scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs`. It must exit 0; supply its command, exit code and output tail to complete_task. On WSL, run it as `env -i HOME="$HOME" PATH="<linux node bin>:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin" node --test scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs` with python3 on PATH and no MOE_* set. The VR rows need POSIX python3: on Windows they skip by the file's existing NOT_POSIX rule, so report where they ran.
2. ALSO run `node --test scripts/tests/local-runner-check.test.mjs scripts/tests/local-runner-snapshot.test.mjs` and report it.
3. Mutants, on scratch copies only; restore and cmp afterwards:
   (i) follow links (drop O_NOFOLLOW from READ inside file_identity, or use os.stat): VR2's symlink rows;
   (ii) walk the whole tree instead of the manifest paths: VR3's mode-000 rows;
   (iii) ignore the exec bit: VR2;
   (iv) accept a second frame: VH;
   (v) verify after remove: CJ9's order;
   (vi) report 'intact' on a verify rejection: CJ9.

ADVERSARIAL SELF-REVIEW, once, as the final step. Load adversarial-self-review. Read the diff as a check job trying to make a modified workspace look intact. Check:
- symlinks, hard links, FIFOs, sockets or devices at a manifest path or an ancestor;
- an unreadable (000) directory, which must be changed, never an error that hides a modification;
- a file growing while it is hashed;
- TOCTOU between lstat and open, through the fd fstat;
- a manifest path the job deleted and then recreated as a directory;
- a huge manifest, bounded by read_manifest's MAX_MANIFEST_BYTES and the materialize limits.
Also confirm:
- no path or byte ever leaves the guest;
- the host never trusts a frame shape beyond {kind, changed};
- the other modes are byte-for-byte unchanged;
- the R11 cleanup ordering still deletes before settling;
- executionReady stays false and verified-local is untouched.
The guarantee is the workspace state at session end. A change the job restored before exiting is out of reach, as in R11b's unchanged(); document that limit in the module comment, never over-claim. Report every path in complete_step.modifiedFiles, and write the Serena handoff memory 'task-task-5b0a2bcf70f34c62ba29df0f7ff99988-handoff' for V04b (task-340a07b3) and R13 (task-f4811a72).
